# madcide keybinding profile: Pico-style single chords — the SAME action
# vocabulary as joe.keys respelled onto the subset that fits one chord.
# The adapter is data all the way down; a swap is one ui::tui_bind_keys
# call. (No ^h/^i/^j/^m: those bytes ARE backspace/tab/enter. Arrows,
# home/end, pgup/pgdn serve motion here — the diamond is JOE's.)
# The style's name in Tools ▸ Key bindings… (plan §41.11a step 3e).
@title Pico

^s save
^q quit
^x discard
^g help
^w find
^l findnext
^\ replace
^b mark
^n bend
^k blockdel
^u blockcopy
^v blockmove
^z undo
^^ redo
^e check
^o outline
^p profile
^y delline
^d delword
^t gotoline
^r insertfile
# F5 runs the buffer into the REPL tab's session: a fresh one, its main
# run, its names left for the prompt (plan §41.10a).
f5 replrun
# The project window (^F here: ^P is this profile's keymap toggle; the
# JOE diamond is not pico's) + its @project keys as DATA (the baked
# defaults add esc/backspace).
^f project
@project ins projadd
@project del projdel
@project enter projopen
